title: Aphorism
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
url: https://www.litcharts.com/literary-devices-and-terms/aphorism

A short sentence or statement expressing a general truth or philosophical observation.

* a pithy observation that contains a general truth (Oxford)
* a concise statement of a principle ([[Miriam Webster]])
* a terse formulation of a truth or sentiment > an adage ([[Miriam Webster]])
* an ingeniously terse style of expression : aphoristic language ([[Miriam Webster]])

Mine tend to be things like [[Waste = Food]] and [[Everything Is Connected]].

See [[Quote]], [[Principle]], [[Manifesto]], [[Oblique Strategies]], [[Slide One Liners?]], [[An Essay: A Definition]], [[Less Is More]], [[Less, but better]]
